  ("How much does heat pump installation cost in Toronto?", "Heat pump installation in Toronto starts at $5,500 installed for a cold-climate ducted system, before rebates. Installed pricing depends on size and installation requirements such as wall brackets, duct changes and the 240V circuit, so we give you a written, guaranteed quote after the site visit."),
  ("How long does a heat pump install take in a Toronto home?", "Most single-system heat pump installations in Toronto are finished in one working day once pre-approval and equipment are in place. Multi-zone ductless jobs, duct repairs or a panel upgrade can add a day. We give you the schedule in writing with the quote rather than a promise over the phone."),
  ("Can I get the full $7,500 rebate if my Toronto home is heated with Enbridge gas?", "Usually not the full amount. The Home Renovation Savings Program pays the top tier, up to $7,500, to homes heated by electricity, oil, propane or wood, while Enbridge gas-heated homes commonly receive up to $2,000. The amount depends on heat pump size, pre-approval must be in place before installation, and program terms can change, so we confirm eligibility with you first."),
  ("Do I need a permit for a heat pump installation in Toronto?", "The electrical work for a heat pump is done by an ESA-licensed electrician and filed with the Electrical Safety Authority, and we look after any City of Toronto permit or property manager approval the job needs. Condo and townhouse owners usually need written sign-off on placement, and we prepare that request."),
  ("Will a heat pump fit a narrow Toronto lot or laneway house?", "Yes. We install heat pumps on wall brackets, in rear yards, on flat roofs where the structure allows, and in laneway houses with careful line set routing. The site visit settles where the outdoor unit goes and how we keep it quiet for the neighbours before you sign anything."),
